{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, d2kq5a_, d3v6pa_, and d4cj9a_ are all SCOPe domains in the same family, a.298.1.1, TAL (transcription activator-like) effector, within superfamily a.298.1 TAL effector-like, fold a.298 Left-handed alpha-alpha superhelix, and class a All alpha proteins. Their lower nodes are different proteins and species: d2kq5a_ is PthA from Xanthomonas axonopodis pv. citri, d3v6pa_ is dHax3 from Xanthomonas, and d4cj9a_ is BurrH from Burkholderia rhizoxinica. The apparent length discrepancy is exactly the repeat-family case: the conserved SCOPe unit is a small alpha-helical TAL-effector repeat, not a fixed-length whole chain, and SCOPe marks d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_ with the repeat heterogeneity code re, meaning that members of the family contain different numbers of small repeating units. SCOPe’s canonical repeat representative for this family is d4cj9a_, specifically 4cj9 A:259-292; that coordinate annotation applies directly to d4cj9a_ and is only a family representative for the other SIDs. Thus the common family assignment supports homology of the TAL effector repeat architecture at family strength, but it does not imply equal repeat counts, one-to-one full-length residue correspondence, transfer of d4cj9a_ coordinates to PthA or dHax3, or that every residue in the differently sized chains has the same template or function.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains: /api/v1/releases/current; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/homology\"]}]}"}}
